{"title":"2004 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Long)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Long)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Faster)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2010 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 4\">Problem 4</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>palindrome</i> is a positive integer that is the same when read forwards or backwards. For example, three palindromes are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/a/76ad7692f5d86be790209a56a68c2a3488235054.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$121$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/5399794b44034434d41f9fc49e73f4966feb8e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7739377$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Calculate the 10th and 24th triangular numbers.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Long.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Long)\">Solution 1 (Long)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Long)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The fourth triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the fifth triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/f/29f4afbb7dbc2e34da654ead3afe88a00fc2dbb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 + 5 = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The fifth triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the sixth triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/f/0ff82e9f84bd6df9c6af21062cb33fd199f83b7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15 + 6 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The sixth triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the seventh triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/2/ba2390bfcc3c167d7f0f4820da54659d205db09c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 + 7 = 28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The seventh triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/6/9265f5dd6dade78136a6be158ace46bf7c0f8ce3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the eighth triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/632d6c748f5a3f759eb769f2e0a66eb803c06ed6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$28 + 8 = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The eighth triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the ninth triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/3/fd3a797546a376cf08c4067fdc198ae9ccd5ac36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 + 9 = 45$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The ninth triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/5/f25d31faf472ddb4c698a14522fe8125c06f8dd8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the 10th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50a9b9cab8a94374813cd2551d1ab9f697a4c3cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$45 + 10 = \\boxed{55}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"114\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>The 10th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79030abeb688469b5ffc2e1c4e37fee225a529e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the 11th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/5/0c53ad310dc5f5e63df3fe4871ae7659db45ee50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$55 + 11 = 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 11th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/4/2d40f3652c1962e98ce050a88c04ed37997c67df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the 12th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/e/c8e8ca5bfcc6ad3e752b971e67ba1f0cba1a5436.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$66 + 12 = 78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 12th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76d15d808807bfa561e72dc8111649ed0a204ebe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the 13th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/5/8c59da72d9315efae1375a3d3718e0f2d00c44f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$78 + 13 = 91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 13th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/d/7fd34ff50f8bba26a08bc96a69e921daa60f5f12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, so the 14th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/e/70e8c5e28bd63bafd94ef0efbca4b2be2622369d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$91 + 14 = 105$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"112\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 14th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/1/791f15f656db201fa9116a2f762a4b292fc50883.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so the 15th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/4/5947fae2a3873b0d7bdea5a9d3f7bf36c6070585.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$105 + 15 = 120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 15th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/a/aaa4de95cc6371d125d5cf773cdd9f9913dd1d8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so the 16th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/d/d0d31896d67ef57e7821baa2a346147e2d3f53af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$120 + 16 = 136$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 16th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/f/c3fa029d8ca802c03e5ae47eaf8f71d686cba1be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$136$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so the 17th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a44815faeb43692dfad1e9ec63e5ee38352e73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$136 + 17 = 153$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 17th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/5/f152e2688863b88e971932e82c28adec9063a05e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$153$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so the 18th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/6/466e1b71a37d989bd1899ffc8937ab4e17aaf928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$153 + 18 = 171$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 18th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/e/92eaed6f9b2d5d243abc1410e348b0e525727ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$171$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, so the 19th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/9/a79482918069f1f4dbc80979d9e235b273e7b676.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$171 + 19 = 190$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 19th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/c/11c1903eedb7c6edd5aaa5fdbb609443458e6b2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$190$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so the 20th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/5/315024fcfb9663dc945362452e37542efcf1635a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$190 + 20 = 210$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 20th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/3/b4328d77715c539955c57ce1aee7b7bc9cdea458.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so the 21st triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/0/7204be2846e5279c4f299a1886aa77ddca5f4128.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210 + 21 = 231$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 21st triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/e/e9ef3bdf416b7c8159ccf647f4a23317745c9626.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$231$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" />, so the 22nd triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/464c3f8c5915a85fd38402c497aaf7a0a513e4ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$231 + 22 = 253$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 22nd triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/5/8350ad56249c4928110c3e8b558ca84a2df815af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$253$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, so the 23rd triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/8/0886afe0971a0a5af7746bf64e0b590f43345c80.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$253 + 23 = 276$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"121\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>The 23rd triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/c/60c4e798513e41c6606ab3be5c2e916da352e066.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$276$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, so the 24th triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/2/1729de60d6e7161ff0a1d70512fc3815c5d00c19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$276 + 24 = \\boxed{300}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"132\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Faster)\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /><sup>th</sup> triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/3/1e3c1b2843479998156575a3d1ecf4712b69195e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + 3 + \\cdots + (n - 1) + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c55fa61f6f77bd5e9dc733cb36e4c7372130dfb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n + 1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"69\" height=\"38\" /> for all natural <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Thus, the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d48281fdbfa9b2c32a68a3b5ebb6797809da55ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10(10 + 2)}{2} = 5 \\times 11 = \\boxed{55}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"215\" height=\"40\" /> and the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /><sup>th</sup> triangular number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/c/42c29cfe28e07dd1ae8c946d1a2725d2e3fb15ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{24(24 + 1)}{2} = 12 \\times 25 = \\boxed{300}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"233\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017203813\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.026 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.051 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 246/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 309/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9113/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   17.515      1 2010_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_4\n100.00%   17.515      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:37017:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017203813 and revision id 285986. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}